course: dictionary
lesson: 8022
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The context, meaning the words around them, tells you which meaning the writer wants. «Bright or reflective clothes help drivers see you in the dark.» Drivers can see you because the clothes send back light, so reflective means able to send back light, like a mirror.
explain: Reflective can also mean quiet and thoughtful, as in the phrase «in a reflective mood». Nobody is shining a light there; the person is thinking carefully. Ask yourself: is something shining, or is someone thinking?
explain: Test your choice by swapping the meaning into the sentence. «Reflective material sends a car's headlight beam back towards the driver» makes sense with send back light. Try quiet and thoughtful there and it does not make sense, so you know which meaning fits.
fact: Reflective means able to send back light, like a mirror.
fact: «Reflective material sends a car's headlight beam back towards the driver.»
fact: Reflective also means quiet and thoughtful, thinking carefully about things.
fact: Reflective strips, armbands and backpack strips help drivers see children at night.
fact: Some words have more than one meaning, so always check the context.
exercise: «Bright or reflective clothes help drivers see you in the dark.» What does reflective mean here? | *Able to send back light | Dark and rough | Quiet and thoughtful | Very old
exercise: Ella says, «She sat in a reflective mood by the window.» What does reflective mean in this sentence? | Shiny like a car's headlights | *Quiet and thoughtful | Wet and grey | Glowing like a lamp
exercise: «In thick fog, wear reflective clothes, walk on the pavement and cross only at a crossing.» Why should you wear reflective clothes in fog? | *So that drivers can see you | Because fog is fun to wear | Because they keep you dry | To look thoughtful
test: «Reflective strips shine the headlights straight back to the driver.» Which word has the same meaning as reflective here? | Thoughtful | *Able to send light back | Quiet | Old
test: Which meaning fits best in «a reflective piece looks back on what you learned»? | Dark and rough | Wet and grey | *Thinking carefully about things | Able to send back light
exam: Mia reads, «The reflective jacket shone in the headlights.» Then she reads, «He was in a reflective mood.» In which sentence does reflective mean able to send back light? | Both of them | *The first one, about the jacket | Neither of them | The second one, about the mood
